  ok   _number(slider=True) passes its increment as step and explicit SLIDER mode

-- E1: setup, reauth and options share one token mask
  ok   the three tibber_token surfaces agree on the same mask
  ok   that shared mask is the password TextSelector

-- user: the same plant twice, a second pump once
  ok   a valid first screen offers finish-setup-now
  ok   and carries the plant identity as the flow's unique id
  ok   the same answers a second time abort as already_configured
  ok   a second heat pump on the same account proceeds (null control)
  ok   a flat identity payload is invalid on the grouped setup schema, the nested one is valid
  ok   a nested user_sensors submit still identifies the plant

-- user: refused and unreachable tokens, required fields
  ok   a 401 re-shows the first screen with invalid_tibber_token
  ok   a refused token stores nothing
  ok   a connect failure shows cannot_connect, not invalid_tibber_token
  ok   an HTTP 500 is cannot_connect, not invalid_tibber_token
  ok   a server fault stores nothing
  ok   an errors payload on HTTP 200 is an invalid token too
  ok   the first-screen schema requires the weather entity, not the token
  ok   Tibber without a token is tibber_token_required
  ok   an entity source without a price sensor is price_entity_required
  ok   an entity price source proceeds without a Tibber token

-- E2/E3: finish-setup-now shows the overview, then creates
  ok   the second screen opens the finish-setup menu
  ok   finish-setup-now shows the setup overview
  ok   confirming the early overview creates the entry
  ok   the early entry carries the first two screens and no later page

-- walk 1 (questionnaire): user through create_entry
  ok   the accepted first screen offers finish-setup-now
  ok   continuing setup lands on temperature
  ok   a valid comfort band opens the building menu
  ok   the band answers are accumulated
  ok   the questionnaire proceeds to the heat pump extras
  ok   the answers are stored and the physics derived from them
  FAIL a fresh questionnaire derives a single-zone model (no zone keys)  [['upper_floor_thermal_mass', 'lower_floor_thermal_mass']]
  ok   the nameplate numbers proceed to hot water
  ok   an unparseable window spec is invalid_dhw_windows
  ok   a window shorter than one planning step is dhw_window_too_short
  ok   a minimum with no deadband below the setpoint is dhw_min_too_close
  ok   a valid hot-water page proceeds to weather sensitivity
  ok   a legionella cycle above the charge limit proceeds with a warning
  ok   the last questionnaire page shows the setup overview
  ok   confirming the questionnaire overview creates the entry
  ok   the entry carries one answer from every page it walked

-- walk 2 (expert): thermal values and zones
  ok   a modulation floor above the ceiling is min_power_above_max
  ok   the thermal page refuses the same inverted power pair
  ok   hand-typed thermal values proceed to the optional zones page
  ok   zone answers proceed to hot water
  ok   and the zone keys are accumulated
  ok   hot water without a legionella cycle proceeds too
  ok   the expert path shows the setup overview
  ok   confirming the expert overview creates the entry with the thermal values

